            <ArticleTitle>Can multi-slice computed tomography of the heart be useful in patients with epicardial leads?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>87-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.5603/CJ.2013.0014</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>New visualization methods are helpful in the noninvasive diagnosis of heart diseases. However, sometimes epicardial and endocardial leads can cause problems due to a large number of artifacts. Based on the presented case, we conclude that it is possible to perform multi-slice computed tomography of coronary arteries despite the coexistence of transvenous and epicardial leads.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
